{"name":"Aphrodisiac","hex":"#e35a63","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aphrodisiac","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Arousing or intensifying sexual desire."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something, generally a food or drug, having such an effect."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aphrodisiac"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aphrodisiac","blocks":[{"text":"An aphrodisiac is a substance that increases libido, sexual desire, sexual attraction, sexual pleasure, or sexual behavior. These substances range from a variety of plants, spices, and foods to synthetic chemicals. Natural aphrodisiacs, such as cannabis or cocaine, are classified into plant-based and non-plant-based substances. Synthetic aphrodisiacs include MDMA and methamphetamine. Aphrodisiacs can be classified by their type of effects. Aphrodisiacs that contain hallucinogenic properties, such as bufotenin, have psychological effects that can increase sexual desire and sexual pleasure. Aphrodisiacs that have smooth muscle relaxing properties, such as yohimbine, have physiological effects that can affect hormone concentrations and increase blood flow. Substances that have the opposite effects on libido are called anaphrodisiacs. Aphrodisiac effects can also be due to the placebo effect."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/1926WantQuickPep.jpg/330px-1926WantQuickPep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aphrodisiac","wikidata":"Q211420"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Ambergris.jpg/500px-Ambergris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Ambergris.jpg/1280px-Ambergris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Ambergris.jpg/500px-Ambergris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ambergris","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmbergris.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Ethanol-3D-balls.png/500px-Ethanol-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Ethanol-3D-balls.png/500px-Ethanol-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A molecule of alcohol","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEthanol-3D-balls.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Insam_%28ginseng%29.jpg/500px-Insam_%28ginseng%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Insam_%28ginseng%29.jpg/1280px-Insam_%28ginseng%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Insam_%28ginseng%29.jpg/500px-Insam_%28ginseng%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ginseng","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInsam_(ginseng).jpg"}],"sounds":{"aphrodisiac":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-aphrodisiac.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-aphrodisiac.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-aphrodisiac.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-aphrodisiac.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-aphrodisiac.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[]}}